    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d750">

                <pb facs="0716" n="704" xml:id="pg704"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.857/66: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-02-29T17:00:00-03:00">February 29,
                            1940—5 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 6 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>76. Department’s 42, February 27, 8 p.m. Aranha says that he would appreciate it
                    highly if the Department as a friendly gesture would circulate the text of the
                    protest on the <hi rendition="#italic">Wakama</hi> incident drafted by the
                    Brazilian Government to the other American Republics and suggest their approval.
                    …</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
